// Targeted therapy: HPV16 E6 oncogene excision in cervical cancer cells.
//
// The virus (AAV) is the drug delivery vehicle. It carries CRISPR-Cas9
// with a guide targeting the HPV16 E6 oncogene. Only cells harboring
// integrated HPV16 DNA are affected.
//
// Biology:
//   1. AAV vector carrying Cas9 + E6-targeting guide is delivered systemically
//      or locally to the cervix
//   2. In cells WITHOUT HPV16 integration: Cas9 finds no target → no cut → no effect
//   3. In cells WITH HPV16 integration: Cas9 binds E6 → cuts → disrupts oncogene
//   4. E6 disruption restores p53 tumor suppressor → cancer cell death
//
// This is sequence-conditional drug delivery: the virus is the vehicle,
// CRISPR is the sensor, and the therapeutic effect (p53 restoration)
// only triggers in cells containing the target sequence.
//
// Real work: Hu et al. 2014, Kennedy et al. 2014, Zhen et al. 2020

target HPV16_E6 {
  organism human
  tolerance 0
  signatures GACCTGTTAGCAATCCG
  in only [ epithelial.cell ] @measured(human)
}

excise HPV16_E6
